Title:
SrHollow — LSA Secrets Extraction via Existing VSS Shadow Copy + Inline REGF Parser + AES-256 LSA Decrypt

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
SrHollow is a Windows post-exploitation toolchain for extracting and decrypting LSA secrets by reading the SYSTEM and SECURITY registry hives from an existing Volume Shadow Copy (VSS) snapshot. It avoids direct live-hive access by enumerating `\GLOBAL??` for `HarddiskVolumeShadowCopyN` devices and, if none exist, can create a restore point via `SRSetRestorePointW`. The project includes an inline `regf` (registry hive) parser in C# and implements the full key-derivation path: BootKey (SYSKEY) extraction, LSA AES-256 key recovery from `PolEKList`, and decryption of `Policy\Secrets`. It also parses `DPAPI_SYSTEM` to recover machine/user DPAPI keys, enabling decryption of SYSTEM-scoped DPAPI master keys. It’s primarily useful for Red Teams and pentesters performing credential/secret recovery on local admin contexts, and is interesting for its low-dependency implementation and “backup-like” file access pattern when a shadow copy already exists.

Technical Focus:
- VSS shadow copy enumeration and hive access via `\\?\GLOBALROOT\Device\HarddiskVolumeShadowCopyN`
- `SeBackupPrivilege` enablement and backup-semantics file reads
- Offline Windows registry hive (`regf`) parsing (cells: `nk`, `vk`, `lf/lh/li/ri`, `sk`, etc.)
- BootKey (SYSKEY) reconstruction from LSA class data and permutation
- LSA secret decryption (SHA-256 stretching + AES-256-CBC via `bcrypt.dll`)
- DPAPI_SYSTEM extraction (MachineKey/UserKey) for DPAPI offline decryption workflows

Use Cases:
- Dump and decrypt LSA secrets (service account passwords, cached secrets depending on configuration)
- Recover `DPAPI_SYSTEM` keys to unlock SYSTEM DPAPI-protected material
- Perform offline credential/secret triage from VSS snapshots with minimal tooling
- Red team tradecraft: reduce noisy live-hive access by leveraging preexisting shadow copies
- Incident response validation: reproduce how an attacker could extract secrets from VSS

Keywords:
LSA secrets, VSS, Volume Shadow Copy, HarddiskVolumeShadowCopy, \GLOBAL??, NtOpenDirectoryObject, NtQueryDirectoryObject, SeBackupPrivilege, AdjustTokenPrivileges, SRSetRestorePointW, SrClient.dll, registry hive, REGF, SYSTEM hive, SECURITY hive, BootKey, SYSKEY, PolEKList, AES-256-CBC, SHA-256, bcrypt.dll, DPAPI_SYSTEM, DPAPI master key, offline decryption, CreateFileW, FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS, PowerShell stages, Add-Type, C# payload